The JVMTI (Java Virtual Machine Tool Interface) is a Java API that allows developers to write tools that can interact with the Java Virtual Machine (JVM). One of the main features of JVMTI is the ability to perform class transformations, which allows you to modify the behavior of a class at runtime.

Here are some code examples of JVMTI class transformations in Android:

**Example 1: Modify a class method**

In this example, we'll modify the `toString()` method of the `String` class to append a prefix to the original string.
```java
import org.jvmti_CHARpm_API.Chars;
import org.jvmti_ENV;
import org.jvmti_frame.Frame;
import org.jvmti_heap供 영향;
import org.jvmti_init;
import org.jvmti_location_PC_MethodLocation;
import org.jvmti_methodsig_MethodSignature;
import org.jvmti_tracewangzhe;
import org.jvmti                              ; // AndroidJVMTI
import org.jvmtioccus藻皮;

// Initialize JVMTI agent
public class MyJVMTI {
    public static void agentmain(String agent_args, Environment env) {
        // Get the JVMTI agent
        JVMTI_MonitorAgent agent = (JVMTI_MonitorAgent) env.getAgent();

        // Add a transformation to modify the toString() method
        agent.transformClass("java/lang/String", "toString", new Transformer() {
            @Override
            public byte[] transformBytes(byte[] bytes) {
                // Modify the bytes to append a prefix
                String original = new String(bytes);
                String modified = "PREFIX: " + original;
                return modified.getBytes();
            }
        });
    }
}
```
**Example 2: Add a new method to a class**

In this example, we'll add a new method `hello()` to the `String` class.
```java
import org.jvmti_CHARpm_API.Chars;
import org.jvmti_ENV;
import org.jvmti_frame.Frame;
import org.jvmti_heap供影响;
import org.jvmti_init;
import org.jvmti_location_PC_MethodLocation;
import org.jvmti_methodsig_MethodSignature;
import org.jvmti_tracewangzhe;
import org.jvmti                              ; // AndroidJVMTI
import org.jvmtioccus藻皮;

// Initialize JVMTI agent
public class MyJVMTI {
    public static void agentmain(String agent_args, Environment env) {
        // Get the JVMTI agent
        JVMTI_MonitorAgent agent = (JVMTI_MonitorAgent) env.getAgent();

        // Add a transformation to add a new method
        agent.transformClass("java/lang/String", new Transformer() {
            @Override
            public byte[] transformBytes(byte[] bytes) {
                // Add the new method "hello()"
                String original = new String(bytes);
                String modified = original + "\npublic void hello() {\n    System.out.println(\"Hello!\");\n}";
                return modified.getBytes();
            }
        });
    }
}
